WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:03.560
<i>No.</i>

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.940
<i>Not one person arrived
at a place like this.</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.610
<i>Why did you seek such a place?</i>

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.080
<i>Why didn't you let this go?</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.450
<i>You'd known it was all a dream.
Why didn't you acknowledge that it's a dream?</i>

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.580
<i>Answer me, Iskandar!</i>

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.380
<i>Hephaestion?</i>

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.590
A dream?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:33.800
Sir!

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.550
He's fine.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.640
He's gotten over the worst of it.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.890
I'm so glad!

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.140
I see. Looks like he failed to die.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.810
You have good skills,
contrary to what I expected.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.520
Is healing magic your forte?

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.440
My forte or not,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.820
he taught me Electrical Magecraft
several weeks ago.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.910
Several weeks?

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.000
I've heard rumors
about the El-Melloi Class, but...

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.170
A Servant attacked you?

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.210
The phenomenon
of summoning a Heroic Spirit

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.250
with its original personality intact

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.930
can't possibly happen
outside the Holy Grail War in Fuyuki.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.010
<i>"Invocation."</i>

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.520
<i>It's Magecraft that takes astral bodies
known as "Heroic Spirits" or "Divine Spirits,"</i>

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.140
<i>and projects them onto yourself
so that you can borrow their powers.</i>

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.560
<i>Oh, sir!</i>

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.230
<i>If you were to invoke the god of manga,</i>

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.270
<i>would you become good at drawing manga?</i>

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.320
<i>Hey, why does it have to be manga?</i>

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.530
<i>The author of the manga I bought recently
at the used bookstore is dead,</i>

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.200
<i>and I want to read the continuation.</i>

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.120
<i>In principle, it's possible.</i>

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.460
<i>Harboring the soul of the deceased on yourself
in an attempt to artificially revive that soul...</i>

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.460
<i>It's what you call "Sibyl's Magecraft."</i>

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>Many sibyls who have
high affinity to astral bodies</i>

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:59.680
<i>are unaware of their links to memories
and consciousness of such bodies.</i>

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.010
<i>So, it's a divine possession
just like Animalism.</i>

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.760
<i>Right.</i>

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.600
<i>Can't you materialize
the Heroic Spirit or Divine Spirit</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.020
<i>and let them go on a manga drawing spree?</i>

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.610
<i>I'll just say that
it's not impossible theoretically,</i>

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:18.610
<i>but securing enough magical energy
to support such a spell is unrealistic.</i>

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.410
<i>Now, about invocation in practice...</i>

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.240
<i>Let's look at the example
of Native American faith in Power Animals...</i>

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.000
That was without a doubt
a Heroic Spirit who has materialized.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.250
Such power can't be that of a Mage.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.010
That's all the more reason
she has something to do with this.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.010
If it was a Servant, there should be
a Master who summoned her.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.480
And perhaps she was the one
who murdered Trisha.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.610
Magical energy needs to be supplied
to summoned Heroic Spirits...

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.110
Any other characteristics?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.900
Hephaestion.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.910
<i>I am the primary confidante of the greatest
King of Conquerors in history, Iskandar!</i>

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.160
That's how she introduced herself.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.290
A Heroic Spirit who was even dubbed
"the other Iskandar"...

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.000
I see. It all clicks now.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.920
You guys didn't come aboard this train
to buy Mystic Eyes, did you?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.050
A Lord who has no interest in the auction,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.010
the King of Conquerors
who once was his minion,

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.180
and the subject who attacked him.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.560
Let's see. So, Iskandar's Relic
has been stolen from you.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.940
That about sum it up?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.650
So it is.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.780
Just like Trisha said, this Lord is fixated
on the King of Conquerors.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.030
I see.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.110
If it's a Heroic Spirit who is regarded
in the same way as Iskandar,

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.080
you can summon her
from the King of Conquerors' Relic.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.790
Does that also mean that her Master
is aboard this train, as well?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.790
That is quite likely.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.540
But about Hephaestion,
it's the opposite of normal.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.960
Opposite? What is opposite?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.720
Normally, Servants hide
True Names when possible

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.970
because they expose
their weaknesses and abilities.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.060
Instead, they're usually called by the class
that the Heroic Spirit is designated,

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.270
like "Saber" and "Lancer."

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:40.610
So, we know the True Name,
but we don't know the class, huh?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.120
What's the matter, Sir Rodin?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.580
There's an anomaly in the train's path.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.210
This is hard to believe,
but someone meddled with the tracks.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.630
This train is headed
toward the Child of Einnashe.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.540
Can we throttle?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.260
The output won't go down.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.850
I see.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.640
Nothing less from my old haunt.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.270
If the Premonition is only a prediction,

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.230
it can't see through incidents
with nothing leading up to it.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.560
However...

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.130
<i>We have an announcement
to all passengers.</i>

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.670
<i>I regret to inform you that this train
has entered the Child of Einnashe.</i>

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:49.470
Wha...

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.260
Einnashe?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.300
You're kidding!
The Forest of Dead Apostles?

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.100
<i>We're sorry for the inconvenience
until we resume course.</i>

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.940
<i>But we ask that each passenger secure
their own safety in the meanwhile.</i>

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.610
What's this forest?

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.860
I'd like to check outside!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.110
Hold on!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.860
Do you want to die? Look.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.000
This forest is screwing up the Leyline.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.160
Let's do it!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:23.960
<i>O noble spirit materializing
the great desires...</i>

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.000
I see.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.630
They're trying to burn off the forest
that the rails are heading into.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.220
But if something like that
can have any effect...

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.600
<i>Receive our guidance
and show the flames of origin!</i>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.940
Even if they call it
the "Forest of Dead Apostles,"

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.480
it's only a byproduct severed
from the main body. This should—

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.180
They strike in reaction to attacks?

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.050
Where to?

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.430
My room.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.980
I'll put up a bounded field and barricade
myself in until the situation is resolved.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.110
That can't be! We can combine forces
to escape or something!

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.820
I don't even know who killed Trisha!

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.940
And doing something about this forest
in a situation like that?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.950
- It would only create more corpses.
- But—

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.700
Let me tell you this!
I'm not your ally or anything like that!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.450
I'll do it myself.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.200
I'm sufficient by myself.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.210
No.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.670
It's better if I'm alone.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.380
Ms. Olga Marie...

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:53.220
Trisha properly taught me
so that I could do things by myself.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.640
More like, are you able to protect
your mentor through all this?

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:10.020
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:24.660
Jean-Mario Supinerra's Zombie Cooking!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.420
Today, let's enjoy cooking whole roasted
zombies together with Jean-Mario.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:30.920
There we go.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.090
And with that,

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.670
we are finished!

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.550
Whoa!

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.930
And the curtain falls on Zombie Cooking!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.810
Cut!

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.150
That was great, Jean-Mario.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.820
Thank you, Kairi!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.070
Is this person really versed
in the affairs of the Clock Tower?

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:02.080
Yeah. Let me introduce you,
Luvia, to Jean-Mario Supinerra.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.450
He's an old acquaintance.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.960
Nice to meet you, young lady.
Leave the media and gourmet in my hands.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.880
First off, how about a meal?

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.880
Delicious!

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:23.260
Lean dry-aged meat
with a perfectly seasoned sauce!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.220
Thank you so much.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:29.520
I added a bit of soy sauce
in the Madeira for the sauce.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.150
Soy sauce is good and all,
but can I get to the heart of the matter?

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.190
Go ahead.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.820
Remember the case seven years ago where
many headless corpses were found in London?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.160
I remember.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.910
No Mage who meddles with the media
would be ignorant of it.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.580
A murder using the same tactic happened
on the Mystic Eyes Collection Train.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.210
I see.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.710
Back then, there were seven victims.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.590
They were all said to have been
holders of Mystic Eyes.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.010
But I don't recall such an incident
being on the news.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:05.510
The Clock Tower put on some pressure,
and so did the Holy Church.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.140
In the media, it was limited
to one or two broadcasts on local stations,

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:13.020
and the tapes of those broadcasts
have been seized by the Clock Tower.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.020
Was the case ever resolved?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.900
Surely, the case has been settled as a result
of joint investigation with the Holy Church.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.660
I'm sure of it because I got the info
from a friend in Scotland Yard.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.410
In any case...

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:26.620
What's wrong?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.960
Well, is this case booming
right now or something?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.790
A girl from Astromancy wanted
to hear about it just the other day.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.800
Can we ask you what her name was?

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.430
Trisha Fellows.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.190
It's as cold as Siberia outside.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.310
I don't know how long we can last
with the heating equipment on this train.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.070
Will Sir...

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:59.490
He seems fine for now, but...

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.750
Hey!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.370
A-A person?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:25.340
Well, I heard that Waver was here,

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.600
so I came by helicopter to watch,

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.230
but a forest suddenly spawned,
and I got engulfed.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.390
I thought I was going to die.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.190
Well, that's...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.400
Such an idiot...

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.200
Hasn't changed one bit.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.910
Still an idiot as he's always been.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.040
There surely are many
easier ways of life for you.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.590
Can I ask you one thing, Ms. Gray?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:02.920
Sure!

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.050
Who injured Waver this badly?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.720
Who other than myself?

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.440
That's...

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.030
I understand that you are busy,

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.690
but we need to talk.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.570
You need us to lend a hand
to move this train?

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:33.580
Regretfully, we must now think about
the possibility of canceling the auction.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:39.420
If that happens, I can't extract these
Mystic Eyes until the next auction.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:43.760
And so, we want our little apprentice
and Caules to help us out.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.340
But how?

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.470
I have a bit of knowledge about this forest.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.470
This location is a topic of conversation
in the Holy Church, as well.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.480
In the Holy Church?

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.020
The Forest of Einnashe.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:00.230
The forest is a thinking, preying organism,
said to perhaps be a Reality Marble

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:04.860
controlled by a high-ranking
Dead Apostle of the same name.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.110
If we can find the main Leylines

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:12.240
and sink in a few guide markers
from our end, we can activate them.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.450
And by doing that,
we should be able to move the train.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:19.630
But most of the Mages are barricading
themselves in their compartments.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.550
That snake lady from Policies refused, too!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.550
She's so obstinate!

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.050
The more we have to fight, the better.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.840
Can you help us out?

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.300
I'll do it!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.600
Ms. Gray...

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.230
Sir will not last being exposed to this cold.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.020
All right. Leave him to me.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.060
Then, can I mingle with you guys?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:46.110
I may look like this,
but I'm a Tuner of Magical Crests.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:50.530
You can't be the Melvin Weins!
The legendary Tuner?

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:53.580
We stand a good chance
with this many people.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:12.220
My body feels warm.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:20.230
The sounds are resonating with our
Magical Circuits and activating them!

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.610
It feels so good!

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:35.410
I improved your Magical Circuits
by about 20 percent.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.660
It should be of some use, right?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.250
Thank you so much.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.790
But why?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:47.050
I go all out in order to witness
amusing things.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:15.700
This is one.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.620
I'll detect all the other Leylines altogether!

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.290
We're counting on you!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.620
Well, I'm feeling really good
thanks to the Tuning,

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.210
so leave it to me!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.920
I'd like to find at least two more
pressure points for the Leylines. Let's hurry!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.210
Okay!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.010
Hey, Gray!

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.680
What's wrong, Add?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.640
Bad, bad, bad!
The bad thing is looking this way!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.270
Run away this instant!

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:40.680
No way!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.850
What's wrong, little apprentice?

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.440
I'm sorry.
Please go ahead without me.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.520
Wait, ahead of you?

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.990
Please! I'll make sure to catch up!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.360
What should we do?

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:53.860
Understood.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.780
That sounds amusing, though.

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:12.210
Oh, you noticed me?

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:13.340
Add...

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:17.340
Dammit, I thought
things might end up like this.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.020
It's unfortunate that
the narrow-minded man is not here.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.150
Why did you assault Sir?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.690
I said it was because I didn't like him.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:33.320
Even then, you must have some
other reason you lured him out there!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.030
Then, you can get it out of me
with that blade.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.320
That's what I've always done.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.240
Not my style.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.160
You stand on the battleground
not for force but for dialogue.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.000
Then, why do you have that blade?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.420
I...

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:54.130
I can't surrender to you!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.640
I just want to speak as equals
and have you return the Relic!

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.350
I see. So, that's your resolution!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:10.060
It seems that previous guidepost
has marked us as intruders.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.110
Leave it to me!

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:12.980
Ta-da!

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:16.150
Yvette's Processed Mystic Eyes,
Burning Flame Version!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.990
Amazing!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.240
But it won't last long!

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.200
Then, run for it!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.000
The next response is from the right!

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.630
A large rock at one o'clock!

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:32.630
That one!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:44.180
I thought warriors were extinct in this era!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.770
But you have good potential.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:50.900
Potential?

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.310
That's right.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:56.860
Your glimmer is trying to cling onto life,
somewhere between life and death.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:01.700
The pain that Sir is going through
has a lot more value than anything like this!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:08.210
Then, you shall give it
all you've got for your loyalty!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.840
I think I'm at my limit soon!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:15.630
- Oh man!
- We're sliding down!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:17.760
Oh, jeez!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.630
This is why we say
the Holy Church is barbaric!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.140
This feels like a roller coaster!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.810
There, in the center of the vortex!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.310
All right!

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.900
We got a response!
The Leyline is activating!

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.830
It really is strange. It's strange.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.590
A spell right on these coordinates?

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.590
Not the floor or the ceiling,

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.510
but it was embedded in the relative
coordinates from the train?

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.470
But if it's something like that,

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.520
someone like that despicable Lord
would've long since found it.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.850
It's reacting to my Magical Crest?

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:18.530
This spell is of the Fellows Family
that branched out from Animusphere.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.360
That's right!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.820
A dimensional pocket
with an Imaginary attribute!

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:26.780
If so, the password should open it.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.540
"Silly Little Marie,
straighten yourself out."

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.340
What is this?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.760
Strange! This is strange!
What's going on here?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.800
What's the meaning of this, Trisha?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.520
Was someone watching?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:04.240
Oh, I'm glad. You found it.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:09.030
Nothing less from the heir
of the Animusphere name.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:16.920
Where's Ms. Gray?

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.250
It can't be!

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:24.340
Wonderful! I didn't think you could
cross swords with me this well!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.260
Likely beyond the boundaries
of ordinary men!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.010
You're worthy of applause!

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:32.350
An avalanche?

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:35.270
It was simply a divided piece
of a monster.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:39.900
With the domination of the Leyline
taken away, it's become unbearable quickly.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:45.650
What's wrong?
If you don't escape, you'll die, too.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:50.830
If I let you escape here,
Sir will be hurt! That, if nothing else...

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.000
Add!

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:56.500
<i>First restraint practically rescinded!</i>

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.250
I guess we have no other choice!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.840
I won't let you get to him!

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.260
How well you bark!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
EPISODE 9: Rail Zeppelin 3/6
A Sibyl, Decision, and Child of Einnashe
